  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="d089-67d0-016d-56b4" name="Kingdom of Poland (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>THE KINGDOM OF POLAND mid 14th to early 16th century (Armies of Chivalry, pp.44-45).

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[The Kingdom of Poland]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Characters up to 25%, Cavalry at least 50%, Infantry up to 50%, Special Units up to 25%. Allies: up to 25% from the Kingdom of Hungary list (no Peasants, War Wagons or Artillery) or the Principality of Moldavia list (no Peasantry or Mercenaries) - documented only. Hungarians, Moldavians (Calarasi) and Tartars (Tartar Warriors) are allied light cavalry entries from the other lists, subject to the Allies &amp; Mercenaries rule.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
